From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: do not echo batch labels and :: comments

With echo on, Windows cmd does not echo a batch line that is a label (":name", including the "::" comment idiom); Wine printed them with a prompt in front, so npm.cmd showed ":: Created by npm, please don't edit manually." Commands and rem lines are still echoed.
---
diff --git a/programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c b/programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c
index 09a70a5..4a9d12a 100644
--- a/programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c
+++ b/programs/cmd/wcmdmain.c
@@ -2717,8 +2717,13 @@ static WCHAR *fetch_next_line(BOOL feed, BOOL first_line, WCHAR* buffer)
     handleExpansion(buffer, FALSE);
 
     buffer = WCMD_skip_leading_spaces(buffer);
-    /* Show prompt before batch line IF echo is on and in batch program */
+    /* Show prompt before batch line IF echo is on and in batch program;
+     * labels and "::" comments are not echoed, as on Windows */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_ECHO_LABELS
+    if (context && echo_mode && *buffer && *buffer != '@' && !(first_line && *buffer == ':'))
+#else
     if (context && echo_mode && *buffer && *buffer != '@')
+#endif
     {
         if (first_line)
         {
